A sequence of colored beads is constructed using beads of three colors: Amber (A), Blue (B), and Crimson (C). The sequence is found to have a specific count of adjacent pairs of beads. The counts are as follows:
- AA: {N_AA}
- BB: {N_BB}
- CC: {N_CC}
- AB: {N_AB}
- BA: {N_BA}
- AC: {N_AC}
- CA: {N_CA}
- BC: {N_BC}
- CB: {N_CB}

How many different sequences of beads have exactly these counts of adjacent pairs?
